    "updated_at": "2025-05-27T16:48:08Z",
    "body": "I'll admit that I did not consider the specific expected behavior when authoring these steps. Without looking into the details, I would've said that the intention was for all of the specified signal changes to happen atomically. However the design of the POSIX and Windows APIs does not permit this (POSIX almost does) and so I think the best option is to define the order in which the signals are set, so that a developer who requires them to be set in a different order can do so with multiple `setSignals()` calls instead.\n\nOut of this, I think there is therefore an implementation bug in Chromium on POSIX platforms, where the set/clear operations for DTR and RTS should not be merged so that they can be applied in the same explicit order they are on Windows.\n\nDoes that resolve this issue?",
